<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7511" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cerbĕrus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-ros</span></b> ), i, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κέρβερος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the three-</i> (acc. to others, the
			hundred-) <i>headed monster Cerberus</i>, <i><span class="en">Lucr. 3,
			10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 24</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Verg.
				G. 4, 483</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. A. 6, 417</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Prop. 3</span></i>
			(4), 5, 44; <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 2, 19, 29</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 11,
			17</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 4, 450</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab.
				151</span></i> (cf. <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 6, 400</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 2,
				13, 34</span></i>); <i><span class="en">Cic. Tusc. 1, 5, 10 al.</span></i>
			—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cerbĕrĕus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>pertaining to Cerberus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">facies canum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					4, 735</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">os,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					4, 501</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">latratus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat. S. 5, 1, 249</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">portae,</span>”
				i. e. <i>of the Lower World</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. Th.
					8, 56</span></i>
			.</div>
